Reason: This loop only adjusts freemap entries that start exactly at `tmp`, but does not handle the case where the adjustment results in a zero‑size entry (size == 0) while the base remains nonzero. Such an entry can later be misinterpreted or overlap with another freemap entry, causing data corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ichdr->freemap[i].size == 0 && ichdr->freemap[i].base > 0) {
    ichdr->freemap[i].base = 0;
    ichdr->holes = 1;
}
Reason: This additional check, placed after the adjustment loop, zeroes out the base of any freemap entry that has zero size. This prevents the existence of a zero‑length freemap entry with a nonzero base, which could otherwise cause confusion in subsequent operations (e.g., matching on base address). Setting `ichdr->holes = 1` signals that the freemap may not be fully accurate, prompting a future compaction to regenerate the freemap.

